$f(3x)$ is a horizontal dilation by a factor of $\tfrac13$ (the $x$-coordinates are divided by $3$); $-4$ is a translation down $4$ units. So:
- minimum $(-3,0)\to(-1,-4)$;
- $y$-intercept $(0,2)\to(0,-2)$;
- maximum $(3,4)\to(1,0)$;
- horizontal asymptote $y=2\to y=-2$ (the curve approaches it from below on the left and above on the right) (see graph).
